{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"pages":{"62521579":{"pageid":62521579,"ns":6,"title":"File:Archway of Old London Bridge RMG PW0767.jpg","index":1,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":662010,"width":1280,"height":1012,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Archway_of_Old_London_Bridge_RMG_PW0767.jpg/960px-Archway_of_Old_London_Bridge_RMG_PW0767.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":640,"thumbheight":506,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/dd/Archway_of_Old_London_Bridge_RMG_PW0767.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Archway_of_Old_London_Bridge_RMG_PW0767.jpg/960px-Archway_of_Old_London_Bridge_RMG_PW0767.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":640,"height":506,"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/dd/Archway_of_Old_London_Bridge_RMG_PW0767.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/dd/Archway_of_Old_London_Bridge_RMG_PW0767.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Archway_of_Old_London_Bridge_RMG_PW0767.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=62521579","extmetadata":{"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:William_Lionel_Wyllie\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:William Lionel Wyllie\"><span title=\"English painter of maritime themes (1851-1931)\">William Lionel Wyllie</span></a></bdi>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"Archway of Old London Bridge<br>\n<p>This etching (in working proof state) depicts men at work on the river Thames, framed by the archway of Old London Bridge. For similar shipping scenes of London bridge see PAD8348, PAF0767, PAE1969, PAF0767.\n</p><p>John Rennie\u2019s elegant structure of London Bridge replaced the medieval bridge, which had stood since its completion at the beginning of the 13th century. It was built 100 feet west of the original site and was completed by Rennie\u2019s son (also John) in 1831. After being widened in 1902-04 to cope with an increasing volume of traffic, it was discovered that the foundations were sinking and it was eventually replaced by a new bridge which was opened in 1973. An interesting fate befell Rennie\u2019s bridge: it was sold to the American entrepreneur Robert P. McCulloch in 1968 and shipped piece by piece to Lake Havasu City, Arizona where it was rebuilt and exists to this day as a tourist attraction.\n</p><p>W. L. Wyllie (1851-1931) was a British Marine artist. Born in London, Wyllie painted, drew, and etched Thames scenes throughout his life. He moved to Portsmouth in 1907, where he continued working, supported the restoration of the Victory and painted the Trafalgar Panorama. Early in his career Wyllie was an illustrator for The Graphic, and he became a member of the Royal Academy in 1907.<br>\n</p>\nArchway of Old London Bridge","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"20<sup>th</sup> century<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P571,+1950-00-00T00:00:00Z/7</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"62805204":{"pageid":62805204,"ns":6,"title":"File:Cannon Street RMG PV2061.jpg","index":2,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":684981,"width":1280,"height":668,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Cannon_Street_RMG_PV2061.jpg/960px-Cannon_Street_RMG_PV2061.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":640,"thumbheight":334,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/Cannon_Street_RMG_PV2061.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Cannon_Street_RMG_PV2061.jpg/960px-Cannon_Street_RMG_PV2061.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":640,"height":334,"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/Cannon_Street_RMG_PV2061.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/Cannon_Street_RMG_PV2061.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cannon_Street_RMG_PV2061.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=62805204","extmetadata":{"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:William_Lionel_Wyllie\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:William Lionel Wyllie\"><span title=\"English painter of maritime themes (1851-1931)\">William Lionel Wyllie</span></a></bdi>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"Cannon Street<br>\n<p>A simple graphite sketch of London Bridge, seen from the east, with Cannon Street station to the right, by the marine artist William Lionel Wyllie (1851-1931). This bridge, built by John Rennie, was completed in 1831 and replaced the medieval structure which had stood since its completion at the beginning of the 13th century.<br>\n</p>\nCannon Street","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"20<sup>th</sup> century<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P571,+1950-00-00T00:00:00Z/7</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"90230305":{"pageid":9023